README.md
    1→middleclass
    2→===========
    …
    7→A simple OOP library for Lua. It has inheritance, metamethods (operators), class variables and weak mixin support.
    9→Quick Look
    10→==========
    12→```lua
    13→local class = require 'middleclass'
    15→local Fruit = class('Fruit') -- 'Fruit' is the class' name
    17→function Fruit:initialize(sweetness)
    18→  self.sweetness = sweetness
    19→end
    21→Fruit.static.sweetness_threshold = 5 -- class variable (also admits methods)
    23→function Fruit:isSweet()
    24→  return self.sweetness > Fruit.sweetness_threshold
    25→end
    27→local Lemon = class('Lemon', Fruit) -- subclassing
    29→function Lemon:initialize()
    30→  Fruit.initialize(self, 1) -- invoking the superclass' initializer
    31→end
    33→local lemon = Lemon:new()
    35→print(lemon:isSweet()) -- false
    36→```
    38→Documentation
    39→=============
    41→See the [github wiki page](https://github.com/kikito/middleclass/wiki) for examples & documentation.
    43→You can read the `CHANGELOG.md` file to see what has changed on each version of this library.
    45→If you need help updating to a new middleclass version, read `UPDATING.md`.
    47→Installation
    48→============
    50→Just copy the middleclass.lua file wherever you want it (for example on a lib/ folder). Then write this in any Lua file where you want to use it:
    52→```lua
    53→local class = require 'middleclass'
    54→```
    56→Specs
    57→=====
    59→This project uses [busted](http://olivinelabs.com/busted/) for its specs. If you want to run the specs, you will have to install it first. Then just execute the following:
    61→```bash
    62→cd /folder/where/the/spec/folder/is
    63→busted
    64→```
    66→Performance tests
    67→=================
    69→Middleclass also comes with a small performance test suite. Just run the following command:
    71→```bash
    72→lua performance/run.lua
    73→```
    75→License
    76→=======
    78→Middleclass is distributed under the MIT license.
